Subject: [PATCH 11/11] clk: qcom: add Khaje clock controllers

Add the GCC, DISPCC, GPUCC, and debug-clock providers referenced by the
captured topaz FDT, with DT clock IDs, bindings, and target-framework Kconfig
and Makefile integration. Keep the required CX/MX voltage-corner supplies;
map the active RPMCC, sleep, UFS, USB, and inter-controller clock inputs.

The GCC common path retains qcom,critical-devices consumers, including the
QUPv3 S1 clock used by the referenced I2C controller. The optional LPASS clock
controllers are not included: no LPASS clock-controller node is enabled in the
captured topaz FDT. The series is compiled in CI (GitHub Actions) against the
pinned 6.12 base, and the device trees pass dt-validate and dt_binding_check;
no hardware test has run.

---

The RCG2 clocks that the 5.15 vendor tree marked as "enable_safe_config"
use the 6.12 mechanism for clocks that may already be configured by the
bootloader: clk_rcg2_shared_no_init_park_ops with safe_src_index pointing
at the CXO parent, which parks the RCG on the safe source and caches the
CFG value instead of reprogramming a running clock. The provider files
also include platform_device.h and mod_devicetable.h, required in 6.12 for
the platform driver and the of_match table.

